":false,"_score_spread":9.5,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.41041635843062807,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":31.6,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.02033180540879332,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":9.9,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.06275165164437714,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":12.4,"_gate_pool_share":-0.32743888003577093,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.028836477460726595,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":39.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.13187068159908544,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.019929229697720225,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":33.3,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0033285089613470653,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":54.2,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.002103769357167754,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":96.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.29292,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Marten Transport, Ltd. operates as a temperature-sensitive truckload carrier for shippers in the United States, Mexico, and Canada. It operates through Truckload, Dedicated, and Brokerage segments. The Truckload segment transports food and other consumer packaged goods that require a temperature-controlled or insulated environment, as well as dry freight; and regional short-haul and medium-to-long-haul full-load transportation services. The Dedicated segment offers customized transportation solutions for individual customers' requirements using temperature-controlled trailers, dry vans, and other specialized equipment. The Brokerage segment develops contractual relationships with and arranges for third-party carriers to transport freight for customers in temperature-controlled trailers and dry vans. As of December 31, 2025, the company operated a fleet of 2,654 tractors that included 2,577 company-owned tractors and 77 tractors supplied by independent contractors. Marten Transport, Ltd. was founded in 1946 and is headquartered in Mondovi, Wisconsin.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Randolph L. Marten | CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 72 | Compensation: $811,305 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $252K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $531 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Marten Transport, Ltd. is a small-cap industrials business with a $982M market cap on $884M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -11% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 2.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 29% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 83% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.830809047415701},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 40% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Financial Analysis: Marten Transport (MRTN) & Its Peers","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/financial-analysis-marten-transport-mrtn-its-peers.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794581931.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.586,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Behavioral Patterns of MRTN and Institutional Flows","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/89/Behavioral_Patterns_of_MRTN_and_Institutional_Flows_111226021002_1794510602.html"